{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>אף ברי</b> — its meaning is: sometimes. Therefore he said: even when the air is clear, the Place [i.e. God] will trouble a cloud." "<b>יפיץ</b> — like יפוצו מעינותיך (Prov. 5:16). And he explained: יפיץ ענן אורו — sometimes the rain falls and the sun appears. And some say: the bet in the word ברי is servile [a particle], and [they] explain רי from רויה. This is far-fetched."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra quotes a phrase יפיץ ענן אורו which appears to be an interpretive paraphrase of the verse's continuation rather than a direct biblical citation; rendered as presented."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:52.961480728Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}